## Recommended order

Start with the prerequisite chapters, then pilot one chapter in `full` mode,
then follow the dependency DAG. Record the chosen order here.

## Per-section pipeline

| # | Stage | Role | Gate |
| ---: | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Ingest | architect | counts match the parser summary; every item has `id` and `source` |
| 2 | Reuse triage | architect | every card has `reuse` in `M/F/S/N`, no `?` |
| 3 | Definitions | architect + statement-smith | `af_check` with zero `sorry`; read-back accepted; `defs.lock` entry |
| 4 | Statements | statement-smith | `af_check` = `OK_STATEMENT`; exactly one `sorry` in mode 2 |
| 5 | Read-back audit | auditor | `readback` non-null; binders/hypotheses/universes confirmed |
| 6 | Sketch | prover | dependency edges and key lemmas reviewed (mode 1 only) |
| 7 | Proof | prover | `af_check` = `OK_PROOF`; zero `sorry`; no new axiom (mode 1 only) |

Mode 2 stops after stage 5. A `statements` chapter never emits `sketch` or
`prove` tasks and never creates a `Solutions/` file for a theorem-like card.

## Definition freeze

Definitions freeze before dependent statements. For each definition:

1. formalize it in `Definitions/Def_*.lean`;
2. compile it with `af_check` (zero `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `unsafe`);
3. read it back against the source;
4. append a JSON Lines record to `chapters/{{chapter}}/defs.lock`:

   ```json
   {"lean_name":"Def_...","file":"Definitions/Def_....lean","sha256":"<hash>","frozen_at":"<iso>","chapter":"{{chapter}}"}
   ```

5. after a change, append a new record and re-audit every dependent card.

`defs.lock` is append-only. The old record stays for history.

## Public mission rule

Every mission is public. `"private"` is rejected by `af_init` and
`af_mission`; `af_status` warns on any non-public mission; `submit.sh` always
passes `"visibility":"public"`.

## Mission mapping

- one mission per chapter: `MLM <chapter> — <title>`;
- one milestone per section, plus one `Exercises` milestone;
- one card per item; definitions first, then theorem-like cards, then exercises;
- `af_mission` writes `missions/<chapter>/proposal.json`, `mission.md` and
  `submit.sh`, and never executes the script.

